,"srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/AggregateExec.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/AggregateExec.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":7370,"endPos":8324,"startLine":190,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":206,"endLineOffset":5,"length":955}]}]},{"comment":"The new implementation of `rawTemporaryName` using `String.join(\"$\", parts)` could lead to unexpected behavior if any part contains the `$` character. This change should be reviewed to ensure that no part can contain this character or handle cases where it does.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql-core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/core/expression/Attribute.java-x-pack/plugin/esql-core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/core/expression/Attribute.java--2061:2298","promptId":"#GZ65S","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql-core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/core/expression/Attribute.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql-core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/core/expression/Attribute.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2061,"endPos":2298,"startLine":52,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":55,"endLineOffset":5,"length":238}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":98,"start_side":"RIGHT","start_line":96,"line":98,"comment_lines":["[][96]","[][97]","[][98]"],"review_comment":["Oh, this is very interesting. Thanks for catching this.\r\n\r\nI\u0027m wondering if enforcing unique names for `PhysicalPlan` outputs is actually the right way to go. It is what we assumed so far, so I don\u0027t wanna depart from here, but there\u0027s also a reason to be more lenient:\r\n\r\nIn PhysicalPlan land, this output method was _technically_ correct, because it represented exactly what the physical operators will do: they\u0027re gonna append the blocks for the added fields to the pages that are processed. The blocks corresponding to shadowed attributes/channels will _not_ be stripped from incoming pages.\r\n\r\nThis means that the output layout technically has duplicate attribute names. This change just hides them and makes them inaccessible during the physical planning stage.\r\n\r\nFWIW, `EvalExec` has the exact same situation. `Eval` performs shadowing, but `EvalOperator` can only ever append blocks, so the output pages actually still contain the blocks corresponding to shadowed attributes."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/LookupJoinExec.java","id":36728,"created_at":"2024-12-10T10:51:47Z","original_position":9,"side":"RIGHT","position":9,"original_start_line":96,"submitted_on_commit":"d3b3dc627eaf45d3a255b1e3e5293fc31b395231","diff_hunk":"@@ -93,9 +93,9 @@ public List\u003cAttribute\u003e addedFields() {\n     public List\u003cAttribute\u003e output() {\n         if (lazyOutput \u003d\u003d null) {\n             lazyOutput \u003d new ArrayList\u003c\u003e(left().output());\n-            for (Attribute attr : addedFields) {\n-                lazyOutput.add(attr);\n-            }\n+            var addedFieldsNames \u003d addedFields.stream().map(Attribute::name).toList();\n+            lazyOutput.removeIf(a -\u003e addedFieldsNames.contains(a.name()));\n+            lazyOutput.addAll(addedFields);","submitted_start_line":96,"submitted_line":98},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The modification in `output` method of `LookupJoinExec` could lead to incorrect removal of attributes if there are name collisions or if `addedFieldsNames.contains(a.name())` logic is flawed. Ensure that this logic correctly identifies and removes only the intended fields. The change simplifies the creation of the `AttributeSet` by directly returning an `AttributeSet` containing only `sourceAttribute` if it is not null, or `AttributeSet.EMPTY` otherwise. However, this change might lead to incorrect behavior if `attributesToExtract` contains attributes that are necessary for the plan\u0027s execution. The original code ensured all required attributes (`docValuesAttributes`, `sourceAttribute`, and `attributesToExtract`) were included in the `required` set. This new implementation could potentially omit important attributes.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/FieldExtractExec.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/FieldExtractExec.java-3459:3521,3531:3561,3570:3607,3617:3633-3459:3547","promptId":"#DV7TB","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/FieldExtractExec.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/FieldExtractExec.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":3459,"endPos":3521,"startLine":92,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":92,"endLineOffset":70,"length":63},{"pos":3531,"endPos":3561,"startLine":94,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":94,"endLineOffset":38,"length":31},{"pos":3570,"endPos":3607,"startLine":95,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":95,"endLineOffset":45,"length":38},{"pos":3617,"endPos":3633,"startLine":97,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":97,"endLineOffset":24,"length":17}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3459,"endPos":3547,"startLine":92,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":92,"endLineOffset":96,"length":89}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/LookupJoinExec.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/LookupJoinExec.java-3425:3513-3425:3499,3512:3574,3587:3618","promptId":"#1NCJM","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/LookupJoinExec.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/LookupJoinExec.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":3425,"endPos":3513,"startLine":96,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":98,"endLineOffset":13,"length":89}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3425,"endPos":3499,"startLine":96,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":96,"endLineO